maCars turns it on). The agreements take effect when the last owner signs; CarmaCars countersigns then.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Cannot draw a signature (for example with a disability)? Call us: an Admin can let you type your name instead.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Form A (the trust declaration) is for cars under the Co-Registrant or Transfer method; Form B (the lease summary) for cars under a Lease method. No witness is needed: they are in the same package. You can also sign one on its own page from Documents.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every agreement is signed on screen, with the e-signature. A copy signed on paper is not accepted (a document you signed on paper before November 2026 stays on file as Signed on paper).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-we-set-up-your-car-for-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">We set up your car for you</h2><p class="gd-p">When our team enters your car for you, you get one email: review the details and sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">No sign-in yet? The email has a link to choose your password. It works once, for 24 hours; after that use Forgot password on the sign-in page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/owner/review</span> (Home has <b class="gd-ui">Review or correct your details</b>). Check your phone and address, and each car: plate, colour, odometer, your insurer and your lender. The terms we agreed are shown too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something wrong? Correct it and press <b class="gd-ui">Save corrections</b>. Your documents are filled in again and we are told. A term you did not agree to: message us before you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Everything right? Press <b class="gd-ui">Everything is right: sign</b> and sign once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-sign-an-updated-vehicle-schedule" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign an updated Vehicle Schedule</h2><p class="gd-p">When we agree new terms for a car you already signed for, you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. Home shows it first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open it from Home or the email. It shows what changes (now and updated) and the date it applies from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the text, then sign the same way as your agreements: tick that you read it, initial the updated terms, tick the two consents, draw your signature and press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b> (a code to your phone or email is optional).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your current terms stay until you sign. After that, your invoices and statements use the new ones from the date. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is in Documents.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-form-c-on-screen-with-your-witness-beside-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Form C on screen, with your witness beside you</h2><p class="gd-p">Form C is the lender or lessor permission for a financed or leased car. It needs one witness, and you can sign it on screen when your witness is with you.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form C on screen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Draw your initials beside each of the three acknowledgments, tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Hand the device to your witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement &quot;I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence.&quot; Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form C</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/documents/form-c/4898eb96-0cce-4efc-9fdd-740b4b4e9ad3</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:790/980"><img src="/guides/img/owner-16-form-c-screen-desktop-faa92983.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="790" height="980"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5.7%;top:13.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.9%;top:55.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.3%;top:82.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-form-d-on-screen-with-your-two-witnesses-beside-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Form D on screen, with your two witnesses beside you</h2><p class="gd-p">Form D is a limited power of attorney, once for all your cars. It needs two witnesses, and you sign it on screen with both of them beside you.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form D on screen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Hand the device to your first witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement &quot;I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence.&quot; Then the same for your second witness.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form D</b>. CarmaCars signs Part 2 at the same moment, and the signed copy is in Documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A paper copy is no longer accepted: Forms C and D are signed on screen only. A form you sent as a photo before November 2026 stays on file.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-government-forms-filled-for-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Government forms filled for you</h2><p class="gd-p">Each car&#39;s registry forms are filled in by themselves from your records as soon as its terms are approved, only the ones its onboarding method needs (013-1155 and 013-0169, for example, only for a Lease through a new corporation). When you add a missing value (your address, the odometer) they are filled in again by themselves. Until we load the official PDF, you get a data sheet with the values.</p><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: the <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b> box lists each one with its status and the date it was made. If we correct a value on a form before you sign it, the form is made again and Documents always shows the current one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Documents. Each form shows <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not signed</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b> next to a form, or <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> on Home (the government forms are one To do on your Onboarding checklist).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each form is the official ServiceOntario form, exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it, with only its empty text boxes filled in. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show the form</b>, check every value and tick that you checked it. Do this for each form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the form, give the two consents and draw your signature. CarmaCars records one signature for each form, with the date, your IP address and your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign the form</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Sign the 3 forms</b>). When every form is signed, the step is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Download the filled form</b> on a form, print it and sign it in ink. Its boxes to tick and its signatures are done by hand, at the registry office or before you go, as we tell you.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">If a value on a form changes after you signed it (we correct your address, for example), Documents shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b>, Home shows one To do to sign it again, and we send you one reminder email. Your earlier signature stays on record.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/documents/forms/4d54a524-c28d-4bc4-8ad3-dd9558100a81/official</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/732"><img src="/guides/img/owner-13-official-form-desktop-48614913.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="732"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.2%;top:29.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>ON00453 (a company&#39;s registrant number) is an Adobe form: open it in Adobe Acrobat Reader (free) to see and print it. Other PDF viewers show a blank page, as they do with the form downloaded from ServiceOntario.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Your on-screen signature is a record that you agree to the values on the form. It is never put on the official form: the printed form has no signature until you sign it in ink. You pay ServiceOntario, the inspection station and the appraiser directly.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-the-agreement-for-your-deal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The agreement for your deal</h2><p class="gd-p">Your agreement is filled in from the terms we agreed with you. We email you a link when it is ready: <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b> opens it in your portal, and you sign once for every document.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement</b>: if your corporation leases cars to CarmaCars. It lists each car with its tier (Regular or Troubled), its monthly lease and its delivery date. Each car&#39;s tier is set once, when it is delivered. You pay CarmaCars no fees. We pay in arrears on the 10th: a car&#39;s first payment comes one full month after delivery, and part months are paid by the day, with the calculation on your statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Referral Override Agreement</b>: if you referred another owner. It sets the override we pay you on their cars (out of our share, never theirs) and what you can see of those cars. Find it under <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>: Sign your Referral Override Agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something wrong in it? Reply to the email before you sign and we fix it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-corrected-copies" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Corrected copies</h2><p class="gd-p">If we find a mistake in a signed copy we filed for you, we file a corrected copy in Documents and email you. You do not sign again. Every signed copy opens as a PDF from Documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-ownership-permit-and-car-costs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ownership permit and car costs</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When CarmaCars files your car&#39;s ownership permit, it is listed here and you get an email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When we pay a cost for your car that you pay under your agreement (an oil change, tires, a repair), its receipt is listed here, you get an email, and the cost comes off your next statement.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing', 'chapter', 'partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand', 'Each insurance company pays an agreed rate a day for a replacement car, by car class. The rate sheet keeps those rates with their history; a rental billed to an insurer takes its rate from it, the insurer''s invoice follows it, and each insurer''s page shows what it was billed, paid and still owes.

## The rate sheet

Open **Money** > **Insurers** (the **Rates** tab).

1. One row for each insurer, one column for each car class (the list in Settings > Vehicle classes). Each cell shows the rate today and, under it, a rate already saved for a later date. On a phone each insurer is a card with its classes.
2. Press **Set** (or **Change**) in a cell. Type the Daily rate and, when the insurer has them, a weekly cap, a cap for 30 days, a delivery and pickup allowance, the kilometres a day and a taxes note (printed on its invoices). Choose From, say why it changed, and press **Save the rate**.
3. A change never overwrites the rate before it: it is a new rate from its date, and the earlier one stays in the history. **End** stops a rate from a date.
4. Add an insurer, or change its billing contact and email, in Settings > Insurers.

> Good to know: A car takes the rate of its pricing class; when the insurer has no rate for that class, the rate of the car''s other classes, in the order of the list. A 2024 Jetta (standard, also a sedan) replaced for an insurer that pays $65 a day for sedans is billed $65 a day.

## The rate on a rental

- Add a rental, Insurance replacement (or Insurer billed later): once the price is checked and the insurer chosen, the daily rate authorized is filled from its rate sheet for the car, with the caps and the taxes note under it.
- A different rate: type it, and Differs from the rate sheet asks for the reason. The rental is not added without it. Empty the field to take the sheet''s rate again.
- The review screen of a request or an offer does the same when you choose Bill to and the insurer: the rate follows the insurer chosen, and a rate typed that differs needs the reason.
- An insurer with no rate for the car: type the rate the adjuster authorized, as before.
- The booking''s Insurance replacement card (Overview and Money tabs) shows the insurer and the claim, the daily rate and where it comes from, Differs with the reason when it is not the sheet''s, the caps, the days covered, what the insurer pays and its invoices.

## Charges to the insurer

VLF (vehicle licence fee), LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC and Waiver Saver are charged to the insurer, a rate a day each, only on a rental billed to an insurer. They have no set price: type the rate the insurer authorized on each booking.

1. Add a rental, Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): under the insurer''s details, **Charges to the insurer** has a box for each, the rate a day before HST. Under each box the amount for the days shows; the check of the price adds each line with its HST. Leave a box empty for none.
2. A request or an offer: on the review screen, once Bill to is an insurer, the same boxes are under the insurer''s details. Save, Send offer or the updated offer keeps them; Bill to back to Renter removes them in the same save.
3. A confirmed booking: the Insurance replacement card lists each charge with its rate a day, the days and the amount. **Change the charges** (or **Add a charge**), type the rates, and press **Save the charges**. Each change is in the booking''s history and the changes to the fees.
4. Each line is the rate times the rental days, plus HST: when the dates change, the amount follows. The insurer pays them whether it pays everything or the rental only.

> Good to know: They never show for a rental the renter pays, and the database refuses them there. They print on both agreements: on Blind Spot''s, VLF in box 43, LDW in 45, T&LDW in 46, PAP/PEC in 47 (each with its rate a day and amount) and Waiver Saver in its box beside Accepted; a box with no charge says N/A.

## Invoices to the insurer

- **Draft insurer invoice** on the booking bills the insurer at the booking''s daily rate (the sheet''s, or the one typed with its reason) for the days authorized.
- The weekly cap and the cap for 30 days lower the amount of a long rental. Billed for the rental only, the insurer also pays delivery and pickup up to its allowance; billed for everything, delivery and pickup above the allowance are the renter''s.
- Each charge to the insurer is a line of its own on the invoice (for example VLF (vehicle licence fee): 3 days at $5.00 a day).
- The invoice line says the rate and where it comes from (for example at $65.00 a day, Example Mutual rate sheet, Sedan), and the PDF prints the taxes note. Send it and record its payments in Money > Insurers, the Invoices tab.

## Billing history

**Money** > **Insurers**, then the insurer''s name.

1. The tiles: bookings, days used and authorized, billed, paid, outstanding, the average daily rate and the days the insurer takes to pay (from sent to paid).
2. Rates by class (Set, Change and End work here too), then the History of the rates: each rate with its dates, its status, why it changed and who saved it.
3. Billing by class: for each class the bookings, days authorized and used, billed, paid, outstanding, the average rate and the days to pay.
4. Bookings: each booking with its class, claim, dates, days, rate (Sheet and the reason when it differs), what was billed, paid and outstanding, and its invoices (each opens its PDF).
5. Choose Picked up from and to and press **Show** for a period. **Download CSV** saves the bookings of the period for a spreadsheet.

## Emails as Blind Spot Car Rental

Insurance emails go from **Blind Spot Car Rental <blindspotcarrental@carmacars.ca>** and replies come back to that address: the insurer invoice, **Email the adjuster**, and Email the renter when you choose Blind Spot Car Rental as the sender on a booking an insurer pays. Every other email still goes from CarmaCars.

> Good to know: The address sends today. To receive the replies, the mailbox (or an alias of rent@carmacars.ca in Google Workspace) must exist.

### VLF (vehicle licensing fee)
A default VLF a day can be set in **Settings** (Insurer-billed rentals: VLF a day; $0 means none). When a rental is first billed to an insurer, that VLF is put on it as one of its charges to the insurer; change the rate or remove it there, like the others. Before the renter pays again, remove the charges to the insurer.

### Adjusters
Each insurer has its adjusters, and an invoice goes to the booking''s adjuster (else the insurer''s billing email, which is now optional).

1. On a booking, in **Insurance claim and adjuster**, press **Edit**. Choose the insurer, or **Not listed: add it** and type its name.
2. Choose a saved **Adjuster** of that insurer, or **Add the adjuster** and type the name, phone and email. A new adjuster is saved with the insurer for the next booking.
3. On **Add a rental**, **Saved adjuster** fills the adjuster''s fields; a new one typed is saved the same way (matched by email, else by name).
4. On **Insurers**, open an insurer: Adjusters lists them (**Add an adjuster**, **Change**).

### What was billed
**Insurers** shows **Billed by insurer and class**: bookings, days, the average daily rate, the rental, the charges (VLF, LDW and the others), HST and the insurer''s total. Open an insurer for **Charged by class**, **Billing by car** and **Billing by adjuster**, and each booking with its car, adjuster and charges.
