## Log an expense from the receipt

**Money** > **Company** > **Expenses**, on a phone or a computer.

1. Press **Take a photo** (or **Upload photos**). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.
2. The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.
3. Who pays: the car''s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick **I paid with my own money** to be paid back.
4. Press **Save**. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every real car has its service items: oil, tire rotation, brakes, tires, the seasonal swap, the safety inspection, the registration, battery, wipers, filters, alignment, fluids and the annual inspection. Record a service once and the bill is made and the timers reset by themselves.</p><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-the-fleet-overview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet overview</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car (sample cars are left out), most urgent first: overdue, then due soon, then cars with no record yet, then all OK.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each car shows what is due next, its odometer, its km a day, the tires on it and the date of its last service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Use Show, Service item, Sort and the search (car, plate or owner) to narrow the list, then press Apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a service</b> on a car to record it without leaving the list.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overdue</td><td>Past its km or its date (whichever came first), or expired</td></tr><tr><td>Due soon</td><td>Within 1,000 km or 14 days of it (each item may have its own; inspections and registration: 30 days)</td></tr><tr><td>Unknown</td><td>No record yet: record the last time it was done</td></tr><tr><td>OK</td><td>Done, and not due soon</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-record-a-service-in-one-step" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Record a service in one step</h2><p class="gd-p">From the overview, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> tab, or a To do line.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tick what was done. The items due are ticked already.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the date and the odometer (filled with the current reading). Type the shop, the cost before HST and the HST (worked out at 13%, change it to match the receipt).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the owner (deducted on the owner&#39;s next statement, owner agreement 11.1; the default for an owner&#39;s car), CarmaCars (a company expense; the default for a company car), a claim (a repair cost on the claim), the renter (a charge at cost on the rental), or no charge.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leave <b class="gd-ui">The bill is in: bill it now</b> ticked to make the bill now, or untick it and press <b class="gd-ui">Bill now</b> on the record when the bill comes in. Add the receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the service</b>. Each item done is OK again, with its next date and km.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An inspection or the registration: type the new expiry date, or leave it empty for 12 months from the service.</li><li>Tires: type the tread depth measured, or tick New tires put on (the old set is retired as replaced).</li><li>Seasonal swap: choose the set that went on and where the removed set is stored.</li><li>An expense entered under Money, Expenses with a car and a service category (Car service: oil change, brakes, and so on) records the service too. Voiding either voids the other.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Void</b> on a record sets the timers back. A company expense is voided and an open owner cost is waived; a cost already on a statement or a claim stays, and the void is refused with what to do.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-tires-and-the-seasonal-swap" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tires and the seasonal swap</h2><p class="gd-p">On the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> tab, under Tires.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a tire set</b>: kind (summer, all-season, winter or all-weather), size, brand, tread depth, made (DOT) and bought dates, where it is stored, and whether it is on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Put on the car</b> swaps sets and keeps the swap in the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Tires are due soon at 4 mm of tread or 5.5 years old, overdue at 3 mm or 6 years.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The swap follows Ontario: winter tires on by December 1 (reminder from November 1), off after April 1 (reminder from April 1, overdue after May 1). All-weather tires need no swap.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Winter tires add-on is offered only on cars with a winter set (on the car or stored), or with no tire record yet. A car on winter tires says so on the add-on.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-the-odometer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The odometer</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The current odometer is the highest reading from handover and return reports, field staff moves, the rental&#39;s odometer out and in, listing photos, the car record, services and readings added by hand.</li><li>Km a day comes from the readings of the last 90 days (else the rentals, else 60 km a day). It gives the date a km interval will be reached.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Add a reading</b> on the car; a reading lower than the last one needs the tick. An Admin can void a wrong reading.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-intervals-reminders-and-blocks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Intervals, reminders and blocks</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Each item&#39;s default interval: <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. Whichever of km and months comes first is due; 0 or empty means not by that measure.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Add an interval</b> for a class or one car. A car&#39;s own comes first, then its class&#39;s, then the default. On the car&#39;s tab, <b class="gd-ui">Set an interval for this car</b> does the same.</li><li>Which expense categories are a service, and the items each records.</li><li>Reminders: one Fleet task per car with what is due, To do lines (cars due, services to bill, cars with no record yet) and one line in the morning digest. No other email.</li><li>Handover is refused while a recorded safety inspection or registration has expired. Block new bookings when overdue is off for every item until you turn it on.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Cars that were in the fleet before maintenance came in start as unknown, with one task each to record the last service. Enter what you know once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-check-in-visits-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in visits (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Long rentals get a free monthly check-in visit: <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b>, the same queue as Fleet&#39;s, customer service&#39;s and field work&#39;s. Program settings, Check-in visits: on or off (on by default), the rental length (28 days), the days between visits (30), the reminder lead (5 days, then one follow-up on the due date), the office slots and where. Each booking has its own switch on its booking page. A visit writes the odometer reading and the tire tread into the car&#39;s maintenance, raises a Fleet To do when something needs looking after, logs damage on the Damage tab with an Admin To do, shows on the booking&#39;s timeline, and the owner sees the car&#39;s condition on their car page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="maintenance-and-service-log-an-expense-from-the-receipt" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Log an expense from the receipt</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Expenses</b>, on a phone or a computer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Upload photos</b>). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the car&#39;s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick <b class="gd-ui">I paid with my own money</b> to be paid back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'your-workday', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.

## The menu

Every office role has the same short menu: **To do** (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one **More** for the rest of your work, **Bookings** (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and **Me** (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: **Send an offer** and **New quote** on Requests, **Add a rental** on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters'' phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.

A **More** page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.

| Function | Your links, then More |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur |
| Sales | Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur |
| Fleet | Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button) |
| Finance | Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills |

## To do

Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.

1. The top shows your function, today''s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.
2. **Next up** is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or **Take it** to make it yours.
3. Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.
4. Customer service and Sales: **Waiting for a reply** lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today''s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.
5. **Every open task**: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.
6. Press **Take it** to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. **Sheet** opens the step-by-step procedure.
7. Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day''s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.
8. On a computer, press **/** to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 48.6 20.2, 2 31.9 52.1, 3 41.7 72.3")

## Work a task

Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.

| Button | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Open the working screen** | Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about. |
| **Done** | You finished it. It leaves the queue. |
| **Waiting** | You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours. |
| **Escalate** | It needs an Admin. Add why. |
| **Hand over** | Give it to someone else on the team. |
| **Add a note** | Leave a note for whoever looks next. |

> Tip: Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.

## Today

1. Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.
2. Press a booking number to open it. **To do** takes you back to your tasks.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 700; address: carmacars.ca/va/today; pins: 1 22.9 24.6")

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. The queue shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Several functions? Switch with Working as

If you cover more than one function, **Working as** above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.

## Your scorecard

1. Open **Me** (the **Scorecard** tab).
2. By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.
4. The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 360; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 1 4.2 39.7, 2 62.5 58.3")

## Clock in and out

Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press **Clock in** on your home page when you start and **Clock out** when you stop. **My hours** shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.

## Breaks and activity (release 35)

Take breaks when you need them: there is no fixed length. Press **Start break** next to the clock (a reason is optional) and **End break** when you are back. The timer shows how long the break has run; after 30 minutes you get a reminder and the Admins see it. Clocking out ends a break. Your breaks are on **My hours**; only an Admin can change one, with the reason.

While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks **Still there?**: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the **Call** button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first (sign it on Welcome or Documents to sign), then the academy, then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show your WhatsApp groups (Sales: CARMA Closers and the CarmaCars Team; everyone else the Team group). Next to each link is your member tag, written for you as "Name - Position" (for example "Darren - Sales"), with **Copy member tag** and the steps: open the group, tap its name, tap your own name (or Edit member tag), paste and save. Join each group and set the tag, then press **I joined** and tick **I set my member tag**: I joined does not go through without it.

Passed the Sales part of the academy while Sales is not your main role? Your home page shows the Sales group (CARMA Closers) too: join it and set your tag the same way.

No progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.

## The weekly townhall

**Me** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call''s deck, the next call time and its link. **Add to my calendar** adds the call every week.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)

**KPIs by week** sits on **My scorecard**: your role''s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.

## Your schedule, hours and pay

**Hours** > **Schedule** shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.

| Role | Schedule |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | 6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off |
| Finance | Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work |
| Fleet | 6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off |

1. Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.
2. You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under **Hours** > **My hours**, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.
3. Finance prepares the payroll under **Hours** > **Payroll**: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then **Send for approval**. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.

## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.

## Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)

- Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval.
- Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.
- Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.
- Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.

## The townhall call in the site (release 50)

The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press **Join the call** on **Townhall** or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then **Join the call** again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.

- **Mute**, **Camera off** and **Leave** are under the video; **Share screen** on a computer.
- **Slides** beside the video follow the presenter. **Previous** and **Next** let you look on your own; **Back to the presenter** catches up.
- **Raise hand** to speak, **Chat** to write to everyone (not kept after the call).
- If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and **Join the call** opens that instead.', 'Your workday', 'The menu, To do, task actions, Today, switching functions and your scorecard.',
