progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call&#39;s deck, the next call time and its link. <b class="gd-ui">Add to my calendar</b> adds the call every week.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> there, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-kpis-on-your-scorecard-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">KPIs by week</b> sits on <b class="gd-ui">My scorecard</b>: your role&#39;s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-schedule-hours-and-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your schedule, hours and pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b> shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Schedule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer service</td><td>6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b>, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares the payroll under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b>: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-townhall-s-30-minutes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall&#39;s 30 minutes</h2><p class="gd-p">The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press <b class="gd-ui">Join now</b> (from 15 minutes before), then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm I am in the call</b> on the Townhall page, or press <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b>: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? <b class="gd-ui">Tell yours</b> under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week&#39;s recording is listed on the Townhall page.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-breaks-quiet-hours-and-the-approval-gate-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet VA&#39;s approval.</li><li>Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.</li><li>Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.</li><li>Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall-card-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall card (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, <b class="gd-ui">Join / check in</b> (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-townhall-call-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall call in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Camera off</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Leave</b> are under the video; <b class="gd-ui">Share screen</b> on a computer.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Slides</b> beside the video follow the presenter. <b class="gd-ui">Previous</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> let you look on your own; <b class="gd-ui">Back to the presenter</b> catches up.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Raise hand</b> to speak, <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> to write to everyone (not kept after the call).</li><li>If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens that instead.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'customer-service', 'chapter', 'your-workday', 'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; **Active** always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Change the car, dates, places, price or extras on the offer screen, then **Save without sending** (or **Send the offer** when it is ready).
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

## A buyer lead from a /buy page

Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with "Find me this car", and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.

1. The lead is in **Buyer leads** (customer service: **Owners and enquiries**), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.
2. If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop''s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.
3. Press **Take it**, then **Update** as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.

> Tip: We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.

## Send an offer to a caller

Open **Send an offer** (or **Send an offer** beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.

1. Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press **Add a new customer**: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.
2. Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.
3. The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.
4. How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.
5. Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press **Send the offer**.

> Tip: An offer that is out is changed in place: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, change it, then **Send the update** or **Save without sending**. No need to withdraw it first.

## New quote for a caller

1. Open **New quote**. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).
2. Choose how the lead came in, then the caller''s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.
3. Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.
4. Press **Create the request**. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1220 1260; address: carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new; pins: 1 72.1 15.6, 2 72.1 41.7, 3 72.1 72.7, 4 63.9 85.5")

## Edit a booking, a fee or the renter

A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter''s details are corrected from the booking.

1. Overview, **Edit the booking**: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction.
2. Money tab, Fees, **Change or add a fee**: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.
3. What is open shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)**).
4. **Edit renter**: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.
5. The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: **Merge into this record** moves everything of the other record here.

> Good to know: Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.

## Restore an earlier version

1. Changed a confirmed booking and need it back as it was? Overview, **Versions of this booking**: press **Restore this version** on the one to go back to.
2. The preview shows the new dates, car, rental charge and total, and what the renter would owe or be owed. Nothing changes yet.
3. Type why and press **Restore version** with its number: the dates, the car, the rental charge and the fees go back exactly. Payments are not touched; a difference is a balance or a credit, as with any edit.

> Good to know: Customer service and Sales can restore while Program settings let staff change bookings, with the same checks as Edit (the car must be free).

## Renter messages and Find a renter

1. **Renter messages** lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press **Send**.
2. **Find a renter**: search by name, email, phone or booking number.
3. To open a renter''s private details, press **Open with a reason**. The reason is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 260; address: carmacars.ca/va/messages; pins: 1 32.6 48.5")

## Add a car for an owner

Open **Owners** > **Add a car for an owner** (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them. Photos are optional.
3. Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and send to an Admin**. The application waits in the Admin''s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.

> Good to know: A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, **Regular** or **Troubled** (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.

## Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)

Open **Owners** (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.
2. **Onboarding photos**: **Replace** or **Remove** (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter, or **Approve** or mark it **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.
3. **Government forms**: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.
4. **Add cars from a list of VINs** for the owner: paste or upload, **Preview**, **Add**.

## Owner forms (Forms C and D)

1. Open **Owner forms**. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.
2. Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness''s signature and name.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 300; address: carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms; pins: 2 68.6 36.7, 3 76.7 36.7")

## Rental agreements are signed online only

A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.

1. On the booking, press **Sign now on this device**. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then **Hand the device to** the signer.
2. Or press **Email the signing link** or **Text the signing link**: they sign on their own phone.
3. The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.

## The booking''s rental agreements

The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.

1. Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter''s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says "Agreement v3 waiting for signature".
2. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.
3. Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer''s policy number) are listed: type them and press **Save the missing fields**. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.
4. Every signature: a code to the signer''s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.

## Check renter documents

The renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.

1. Open the task "identity documents or coverage proof to review", or open the booking: **Review** shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.
2. Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.
3. Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back''s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.
6. Need to look again at a document already decided, or at a page of the proof of coverage? Press **View** beside it: it opens for one minute and the view is logged. After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Good to know: The name on the card (release 48). Names are compared the way people write them: a middle name, an initial, a shorter first name, accents, order and hyphens do not matter. A card that still differs never blocks the booking: you get the To do **Check the name on the card**. Check the card and the licence, then press **Accept this card** in the coverage part and write a short reason (it goes in the booking history), or contact the renter. A typed signature whose name differs comes as **Check a typed signature**: check the licence and correct the name if needed. An Admin can turn the card rule off in Program settings, **Card in the renter''s name**.

> Tip: Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin > To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.

> Good to know: Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver''s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.


**Approve all (n)** counts only what it can approve right now (release 48). A proof of coverage that is missing a page is not counted: under Coverage it says **Waiting for the renter** and names the page (their pink slip, or the OPCF 27 endorsement page of their policy), and each page sent is labelled. The renter''s checklist asks for exactly that page, with an example picture, so there is nothing to chase by hand. The Protection Plan is counted once the booking is paid.
## Which credit cards include rental car coverage?

Renters ask this often. **Renters** > **Card coverage** (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.

1. Send the renter `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage`: each card''s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.
2. Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car''s model year and trim so they can check.
3. Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card''s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.
4. Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.

> Tip: A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer''s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings > Card coverage.

## Review requests

Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. **Renters** > **Review requests** shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.

1. On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.
2. The renter should be asked now anyway? Press **Send anyway**. Should never be asked? Press **Do not ask**.
3. Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows "possible match". Press **Confirm** if it is them, **Not this renter** if not, or **Match to a booking** with the booking number.
4. A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press **Add a customer review** and type the customer''s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.
5. On a booking, the card Review requests has **Ask for a review** (for example after a call that went well) and **Mark reviewed** when the renter says they already left one.

> Tip: Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.

## A change to a confirmed booking

On a booking''s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.

## A late return

A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to **Extend** first. Otherwise work it in order:

| Button | When |
| --- | --- |
| **Log a call** | Record each call to the renter and what they said. |
| **Send T13** | The first late notice email. |
| **Send T14 (final notice)** | The final notice. |
| **Request disable** | Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car. |
| **Open an incident** | When the car is not coming back as planned. |

## Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)

A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows **Booked, payment due** and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a **Booked, payment due** To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter''s view is right under **Send the offer**.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## Change protection (release 41)

On the booking page, the **Protection** card at the top has one button: **Change protection**.

1. Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter''s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.
2. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.

Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (**Change protection**) uses the car''s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes.

When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: **Approve**, or **Decline** with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.

## Unanswered

**More customer service** > **Unanswered**: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## Book instantly or Request to book (release 50)

Renters choose on the car page and in the booking form. **Request to book** lands in your requests as always. A request with the chip **Asked to book instantly** is a Gold renter whose instant booking could not go through (the reason shows on hover): answer it first, with a pay link or an offer.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time**: a Platinum renter''s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s booking for it.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Automatic answers (release 36)

Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. **Renter messages** > **Automatic answers** shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, **Answer** and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.

## The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)

On **Review documents** for a booking:

1. **Option 2**: **Card picked** names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and **Card check** says whether it covers this car: *Covers this car*, *Check it* (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or *Does NOT cover this car* with the reason. **Approve** is refused while the card does not cover the car.
2. **Option 1**: each page says what it is: **pink slip** or **OPCF 27 endorsement page**. **Approve** is refused until both are in. **Reject** needs the reason the renter sees.
3. A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.

> Tip: Uploading a renter''s insurance yourself? In **Upload a document**, choose **Which page**: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.

## Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)

- Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter''s, lead''s and booking''s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.
- Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.
- Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.
- The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

On **Leads**, press **The person** on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the **Signals** timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter''s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Long-term rentals paid weekly

A renter who pays week by week keeps the car until they give notice. On the booking''s **Long-term, paid weekly** card, **Turn on** (customer service, finance and fleet). Each week, **Record a payment** for the rental: the amount is the next week''s price and the return moves 7 days. 48 hours before the return with the week unpaid, the renter gets the pay link and an Admin a To do. When the renter gives notice, **End rental on** with the last day.

## Where a lead came from, and duplicates (release 48)

On **Leads**, each card says where the person came from (ChatGPT, Google search and its terms, an ad, direct) and the first page they opened. A person who wrote twice is one lead: a new form joins their open lead by itself, and "possible duplicate: merge" on a card opens the lead with **Merge** and **Different person**. The steps are in the Sales chapter, "Where a lead came from" and "Duplicate leads".

## Check-in visits (release 50)

Renters on long rentals get a reminder to bring the car in for a free monthly check-in visit, and pick a time in their portal (at the office or by request). You see the same queue as Fleet under **Renters** > **Check-in visits**: answer questions, book a time for a renter who calls (**Book a time for the renter**), and switch visits off for a booking on its booking page if the renter asks. Never tell a renter it is required or that it costs anything.
', 'Customer service', 'Requests and offers, new quotes, renter messages, find a renter, owner forms, late returns.',
  'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; **Active** always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Change the car, dates, places, price or extras on the offer screen, then **Save without sending** (or **Send the offer** when it is ready).
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

## A buyer lead from a /buy page

Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with "Find me this car", and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.

1. The lead is in **Buyer leads** (customer service: **Owners and enquiries**), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.
2. If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop''s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.
3. Press **Take it**, then **Update** as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.

> Tip: We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.

## Send an offer to a caller

Open **Send an offer** (or **Send an offer** beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.

1. Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press **Add a new customer**: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.
2. Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.
3. The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.
4. How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.
5. Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press **Send the offer**.

> Tip: An offer that is out is changed in place: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, change it, then **Send the update** or **Save without sending**. No need to withdraw it first.

## New quote for a caller

1. Open **New quote**. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).
2. Choose how the lead came in, then the caller''s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.
3. Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.
4. Press **Create the request**. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1220 1260; address: carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new; pins: 1 72.1 15.6, 2 72.1 41.7, 3 72.1 72.7, 4 63.9 85.5")

## Edit a booking, a fee or the renter

A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter''s details are corrected from the booking.

1. Overview, **Edit the booking**: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction.
2. Money tab, Fees, **Change or add a fee**: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.
3. What is open shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)**).
4. **Edit renter**: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.
5. The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: **Merge into this record** moves everything of the other record here.

> Good to know: Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.

## Restore an earlier version

1. Changed a confirmed booking and need it back as it was? Overview, **Versions of this booking**: press **Restore this version** on the one to go back to.
2. The preview shows the new dates, car, rental charge and total, and what the renter would owe or be owed. Nothing changes yet.
3. Type why and press **Restore version** with its number: the dates, the car, the rental charge and the fees go back exactly. Payments are not touched; a difference is a balance or a credit, as with any edit.

> Good to know: Customer service and Sales can restore while Program settings let staff change bookings, with the same checks as Edit (the car must be free).

## Renter messages and Find a renter

1. **Renter messages** lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press **Send**.
2. **Find a renter**: search by name, email, phone or booking number.
3. To open a renter''s private details, press **Open with a reason**. The reason is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 260; address: carmacars.ca/va/messages; pins: 1 32.6 48.5")

## Add a car for an owner

Open **Owners** > **Add a car for an owner** (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them. Photos are optional.
3. Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and send to an Admin**. The application waits in the Admin''s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.

> Good to know: A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, **Regular** or **Troubled** (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.

## Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)

Open **Owners** (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.
2. **Onboarding photos**: **Replace** or **Remove** (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter, or **Approve** or mark it **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.
3. **Government forms**: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.
4. **Add cars from a list of VINs** for the owner: paste or upload, **Preview**, **Add**.

## Owner forms (Forms C and D)

1. Open **Owner forms**. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.
2. Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness''s signature and name.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 300; address: carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms; pins: 2 68.6 36.7, 3 76.7 36.7")

## Rental agreements are signed online only

A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.

1. On the booking, press **Sign now on this device**. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then **Hand the device to** the signer.
2. Or press **Email the signing link** or **Text the signing link**: they sign on their own phone.
3. The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.

## The booking''s rental agreements

The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.

1. Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter''s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says "Agreement v3 waiting for signature".
2. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.
3. Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer''s policy number) are listed: type them and press **Save the missing fields**. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.
4. Every signature: a code to the signer''s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.

## Check renter documents

The renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.

1. Open the task "identity documents or coverage proof to review", or open the booking: **Review** shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.
2. Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.
3. Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back''s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.
6. Need to look again at a document already decided, or at a page of the proof of coverage? Press **View** beside it: it opens for one minute and the view is logged. After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Good to know: The name on the card (release 48). Names are compared the way people write them: a middle name, an initial, a shorter first name, accents, order and hyphens do not matter. A card that still differs never blocks the booking: you get the To do **Check the name on the card**. Check the card and the licence, then press **Accept this card** in the coverage part and write a short reason (it goes in the booking history), or contact the renter. A typed signature whose name differs comes as **Check a typed signature**: check the licence and correct the name if needed. An Admin can turn the card rule off in Program settings, **Card in the renter''s name**.

> Tip: Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin > To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.

> Good to know: Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver''s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.


**Approve all (n)** counts only what it can approve right now (release 48). A proof of coverage that is missing a page is not counted: under Coverage it says **Waiting for the renter** and names the page (their pink slip, or the OPCF 27 endorsement page of their policy), and each page sent is labelled. The renter''s checklist asks for exactly that page, with an example picture, so there is nothing to chase by hand. The Protection Plan is counted once the booking is paid.
## Which credit cards include rental car coverage?

Renters ask this often. **Renters** > **Card coverage** (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.

1. Send the renter `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage`: each card''s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.
2. Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car''s model year and trim so they can check.
3. Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card''s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.
4. Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.

> Tip: A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer''s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings > Card coverage.

## Review requests

Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. **Renters** > **Review requests** shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.

1. On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.
2. The renter should be asked now anyway? Press **Send anyway**. Should never be asked? Press **Do not ask**.
3. Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows "possible match". Press **Confirm** if it is them, **Not this renter** if not, or **Match to a booking** with the booking number.
4. A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press **Add a customer review** and type the customer''s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.
5. On a booking, the card Review requests has **Ask for a review** (for example after a call that went well) and **Mark reviewed** when the renter says they already left one.

> Tip: Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.

## A change to a confirmed booking

On a booking''s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.

## A late return

A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to **Extend** first. Otherwise work it in order:

| Button | When |
| --- | --- |
| **Log a call** | Record each call to the renter and what they said. |
| **Send T13** | The first late notice email. |
| **Send T14 (final notice)** | The final notice. |
| **Request disable** | Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car. |
| **Open an incident** | When the car is not coming back as planned. |

## Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)

A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows **Booked, payment due** and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a **Booked, payment due** To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter''s view is right under **Send the offer**.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## Change protection (release 41)

On the booking page, the **Protection** card at the top has one button: **Change protection**.

1. Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter''s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.
2. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.

Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (**Change protection**) uses the car''s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes.

When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: **Approve**, or **Decline** with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.

## Unanswered

**More customer service** > **Unanswered**: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## Book instantly or Request to book (release 50)

Renters choose on the car page and in the booking form. **Request to book** lands in your requests as always. A request with the chip **Asked to book instantly** is a Gold renter whose instant booking could not go through (the reason shows on hover): answer it first, with a pay link or an offer.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time**: a Platinum renter''s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s booking for it.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Automatic answers (release 36)

Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. **Renter messages** > **Automatic answers** shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, **Answer** and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.

## The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)

On **Review documents** for a booking:

1. **Option 2**: **Card picked** names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and **Card check** says whether it covers this car: *Covers this car*, *Check it* (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or *Does NOT cover this car* with the reason. **Approve** is refused while the card does not cover the car.
2. **Option 1**: each page says what it is: **pink slip** or **OPCF 27 endorsement page**. **Approve** is refused until both are in. **Reject** needs the reason the renter sees.
3. A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.

> Tip: Uploading a renter''s insurance yourself? In **Upload a document**, choose **Which page**: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.

## Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)

- Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter''s, lead''s and booking''s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.
- Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.
- Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.
- The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

On **Leads**, press **The person** on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the **Signals** timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter''s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Long-term rentals paid weekly

A renter who pays week by week keeps the car until they give notice. On the booking''s **Long-term, paid weekly** card, **Turn on** (customer service, finance and fleet). Each week, **Record a payment** for the rental: the amount is the next week''s price and the return moves 7 days. 48 hours before the return with the week unpaid, the renter gets the pay link and an Admin a To do. When the renter gives notice, **End rental on** with the last day.

## Where a lead came from, and duplicates (release 48)

On **Leads**, each card says where the person came from (ChatGPT, Google search and its terms, an ad, direct) and the first page they opened. A person who wrote twice is one lead: a new form joins their open lead by itself, and "possible duplicate: merge" on a card opens the lead with **Merge** and **Different person**. The steps are in the Sales chapter, "Where a lead came from" and "Duplicate leads".

## Check-in visits (release 50)

Renters on long rentals get a reminder to bring the car in for a free monthly check-in visit, and pick a time in their portal (at the office or by request). You see the same queue as Fleet under **Renters** > **Check-in visits**: answer questions, book a time for a renter who calls (**Book a time for the renter**), and switch visits off for a booking on its booking page if the renter asks. Never tell a renter it is required or that it costs anything.


## Ownership documents in bulk

**More customer service** or **More fleet** > **Listings** > **Ownership documents**

1. Press **Choose the files** and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.
2. Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press **File it on this car**. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.
3. A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press **File it on this car**, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter&#39;s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-answer-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; <b class="gd-ui">Active</b> always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car&#39;s photo, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the licence and one button (<b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Follow up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.1%;top:17.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.8%;top:32.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Change the car, dates, places, price or extras on the offer screen, then <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b> when it is ready).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message and press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>. Within your limit you can also use <b class="gd-ui">Approve (within my limit)</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Approve and send the pay link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:69.4%;top:24%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.8%;top:98%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the &quot;First reply in opening hours&quot; measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: the others see &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows &quot;Opens to you at&quot; a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-an-enquiry-on-an-example-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An enquiry on an example car</h2><p class="gd-p">Some cars on the site are marked &quot;Example car&quot;: samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after <b class="gd-ui">Free:</b> (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-request-from-a-vehicle-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request from a vehicle page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message (&quot;About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE&quot;) and an Enquiry task in To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-buyer-lead-from-a-buy-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A buyer lead from a /buy page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with &quot;Find me this car&quot;, and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The lead is in <b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b> (customer service: <b class="gd-ui">Owners and enquiries</b>), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop&#39;s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-to-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer to a caller</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a new customer</b>: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An offer that is out is changed in place: <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, change it, then <b class="gd-ui">Send the update</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b>. No need to withdraw it first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-new-quote-for-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New quote for a caller</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the lead came in, then the caller&#39;s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Create the request</b>. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1220/1260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1220" height="1260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:15.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:41.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:72.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:63.9%;top:85.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-edit-a-booking-a-fee-or-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking, a fee or the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter&#39;s details are corrected from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Money tab, Fees, <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves everything of the other record here.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-restore-an-earlier-version" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Restore an earlier version</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changed a confirmed booking and need it back as it was? Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Versions of this booking</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Restore this version</b> on the one to go back to.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The preview shows the new dates, car, rental charge and total, and what the renter would owe or be owed. Nothing changes yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type why and press <b class="gd-ui">Restore version</b> with its number: the dates, the car, the rental charge and the fees go back exactly. Payments are not touched; a difference is a balance or a credit, as with any edit.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Customer service and Sales can restore while Program settings let staff change bookings, with the same checks as Edit (the car must be free).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-renter-messages-and-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter messages and Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>: search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To open a renter&#39;s private details, press <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>. The reason is kept in the access log.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:48.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them. Photos are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and send to an Admin</b>. The application waits in the Admin&#39;s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then Route <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owners-the-checklist-the-photos-and-the-forms-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter, or <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or mark it <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b> for the owner: paste or upload, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owner-forms-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner forms (Forms C and D)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness&#39;s signature and name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/300"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="300"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.6%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-rental-agreements-are-signed-online-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements are signed online only</h2><p class="gd-p">A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> the signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>: they sign on their own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-booking-s-rental-agreements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The booking&#39;s rental agreements</h2><p class="gd-p">The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter&#39;s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer&#39;s policy number) are listed: type them and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every signature: a code to the signer&#39;s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-renter-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check renter documents</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task &quot;identity documents or coverage proof to review&quot;, or open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Review</b> shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back&#39;s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver&#39;s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Need to look again at a document already decided, or at a page of the proof of coverage? Press <b class="gd-ui">View</b> beside it: it opens for one minute and the view is logged. After the 90-day removal it reads <b class="gd-ui">Removed on</b> and the date.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The name on the card (release 48). Names are compared the way people write them: a middle name, an initial, a shorter first name, accents, order and hyphens do not matter. A card that still differs never blocks the booking: you get the To do <b class="gd-ui">Check the name on the card</b>. Check the card and the licence, then press <b class="gd-ui">Accept this card</b> in the coverage part and write a short reason (it goes in the booking history), or contact the renter. A typed signature whose name differs comes as <b class="gd-ui">Check a typed signature</b>: check the licence and correct the name if needed. An Admin can turn the card rule off in Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Card in the renter&#39;s name</b>.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin &gt; To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver&#39;s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Approve all (n)</b> counts only what it can approve right now (release 48). A proof of coverage that is missing a page is not counted: under Coverage it says <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for the renter</b> and names the page (their pink slip, or the OPCF 27 endorsement page of their policy), and each page sent is labelled. The renter&#39;s checklist asks for exactly that page, with an example picture, so there is nothing to chase by hand. The Protection Plan is counted once the booking is paid.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which credit cards include rental car coverage?</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters ask this often. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Send the renter <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span>: each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car&#39;s model year and trim so they can check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card&#39;s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer&#39;s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings &gt; Card coverage.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Review requests</b> shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The renter should be asked now anyway? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b>. Should never be asked? Press <b class="gd-ui">Do not ask</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows &quot;possible match&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> if it is them, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> if not, or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b> with the booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> and type the customer&#39;s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, the card Review requests has <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> (for example after a call that went well) and <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> when the renter says they already left one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> first. Otherwise work it in order:</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Log a call</b></td><td>Record each call to the renter and what they said.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b></td><td>The first late notice email.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T14 (final notice)</b></td><td>The final notice.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Request disable</b></td><td>Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open an incident</b></td><td>When the car is not coming back as planned.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-booked-when-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter&#39;s view is right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-book-it-now-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone&quot;. It shows a card; <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-change-protection-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change protection (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, the <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b> card at the top has one button: <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter&#39;s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (<b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>) uses the car&#39;s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes.</p><p class="gd-p">When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More customer service</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-request-as-sent-and-every-offer-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request as sent and every offer (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Original request, as the renter sent it</b> shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. <b class="gd-ui">Offer history</b> lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To go back to an old version, press <b class="gd-ui">Revert to this offer</b> on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Coverage</b> line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-in-three-steps-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer in three steps (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Car and dates</b>: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price</b>: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout&#39;s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and send</b>: what changed, the message and how the link goes.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-book-instantly-or-request-to-book-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book instantly or Request to book (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters choose on the car page and in the booking form. <b class="gd-ui">Request to book</b> lands in your requests as always. A request with the chip <b class="gd-ui">Asked to book instantly</b> is a Gold renter whose instant booking could not go through (the reason shows on hover): answer it first, with a pay link or an offer.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-owner-s-own-trip-instant-bookings-and-book-it-now-releas" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner&#39;s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s own trip ($0)</b>: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Instant (repeat renter)</b>: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter&#39;s instant booking away from the booking page.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b>: a Platinum renter&#39;s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter&#39;s booking for it.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Book it now</b> pressed by staff waits for an Admin&#39;s one-tap approval.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking shows the renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b> when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes <b class="gd-ui">rideshare documents</b> (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-automatic-answers-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Automatic answers (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p">Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. <b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Automatic answers</b> shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-card-the-renter-picked-and-the-two-opcf-27-pages-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b> for a booking:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Option 2</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Card picked</b> names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and <b class="gd-ui">Card check</b> says whether it covers this car: <em>Covers this car</em>, <em>Check it</em> (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or <em>Does NOT cover this car</em> with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> is refused while the card does not cover the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Option 1</b>: each page says what it is: <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> or <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> is refused until both are in. <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b> needs the reason the renter sees.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Uploading a renter&#39;s insurance yourself? In <b class="gd-ui">Upload a document</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Which page</b>: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-calls-auto-replies-and-coverage-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter&#39;s, lead&#39;s and booking&#39;s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.</li><li>Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.</li><li>Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.</li><li>Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.</li><li>The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-person-behind-the-lead-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The person behind the lead (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">The person</b> on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the <b class="gd-ui">Signals</b> timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter&#39;s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-long-term-rentals-paid-weekly" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Long-term rentals paid weekly</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter who pays week by week keeps the car until they give notice. On the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Long-term, paid weekly</b> card, <b class="gd-ui">Turn on</b> (customer service, finance and fleet). Each week, <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b> for the rental: the amount is the next week&#39;s price and the return moves 7 days. 48 hours before the return with the week unpaid, the renter gets the pay link and an Admin a To do. When the renter gives notice, <b class="gd-ui">End rental on</b> with the last day.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-where-a-lead-came-from-and-duplicates-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where a lead came from, and duplicates (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, each card says where the person came from (ChatGPT, Google search and its terms, an ad, direct) and the first page they opened. A person who wrote twice is one lead: a new form joins their open lead by itself, and &quot;possible duplicate: merge&quot; on a card opens the lead with <b class="gd-ui">Merge</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Different person</b>. The steps are in the Sales chapter, &quot;Where a lead came from&quot; and &quot;Duplicate leads&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-in-visits-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in visits (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters on long rentals get a reminder to bring the car in for a free monthly check-in visit, and pick a time in their portal (at the office or by request). You see the same queue as Fleet under <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b>: answer questions, book a time for a renter who calls (<b class="gd-ui">Book a time for the renter</b>), and switch visits off for a booking on its booking page if the renter asks. Never tell a renter it is required or that it costs anything.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-ownership-documents-in-bulk" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ownership documents in bulk</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More customer service</b> or <b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Ownership documents</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Choose the files</b> and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">File it on this car</b>. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press <b class="gd-ui">File it on this car</b>, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'finance', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-requests', 'You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. **Money** opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: **To handle** (payments, deposits, refunds), **By day** (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), **All payments**, **Refunds**, **Deposits**, **Reconciliation** and **Unlinked Stripe** (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking''s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking''s payment). **Owner money** lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.

## Your queue

Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.

![The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.](/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 20.3 24.3")

## Payments by day

**Money**, the **By day** tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.

1. Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.
3. At the end of the day count the drawer and press **Record the count**. The difference shows "balanced", or "over" or "short" with the amount.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.

## Payments, deposits, refunds

**Money**, the **To handle** tab.

1. Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank''s reason.
2. Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.
3. Refunds in progress. Press **Request the refund** and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then **Issue the refund**.
4. Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 865; address: carmacars.ca/va/money; pins: 1 10.6 60.3, 2 72.4 21.6, 3 73.2 33.8, 4 11.0 45.9")

## A payment received another way

An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.

1. Owner invoice: on **Payments, deposits, refunds**, find it under Owner invoices owing and press **Record payment**.
2. Renter: beside the failed payment, press **Paid another way**. Or open the booking''s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.
3. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.
4. Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press **Record payment**.

The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.

Each month''s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.


A pay link for the rental, the fees or the balance asks for what is owed and never more (release 48): the booking''s total less every payment of it, refunds counted back. After a change to the total, the link is for the difference. A booking paid in full gets no balance link: anything on top is a later charge, with its reason. A new link replaces any open one for the booking''s money, and a link still open when a payment lands is cancelled by itself (the booking history says so), so the renter is never charged twice.
## Cards, holds and deposits given back

On the booking''s Money tab.

1. After the return, **Charge the renter**: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press **Charge $...**. Before the return, Rental charges, **A later charge**, with the same reason list on the renter''s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, **Charge the card on file as the deposit**.
2. A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or **Release**. **Hold expired**: nothing can be kept from it; press **Charge the card on file instead** (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.
3. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

## Settle a deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (**Keep the whole deposit (damage)**) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## Read a toll notice

1. Open **Tolls and tickets** and press **Read a notice**.
2. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.
3. Press **Read it**. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.
4. Press **Checked against the notice** on each line (**Leave out** to skip one), then **Save as checked** and **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read; pins: 2 19.5 44.1, 3 4.1 64.8, 4 4.1 89.7")

> Tip: In the work queue, **Match again** retries the match after a fix, and **Dispute** marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.

![The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice''s plate, date, amount and match.](/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls; pins: 1 23.6 12.2")

## Reconciliation and Turo trips

1. **Money**, the **Reconciliation** tab: press **Record a processor payout**, then **Match** it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.
2. **Turo trips**: press **Add a trip** for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press **Import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/turo; pins: 2 95.1 14.8")

## Deposits to release

A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: "Release the deposit for" the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.

1. Open the task: it opens the booking''s **Money** tab.
2. Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.
3. The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.

### Card payments outside the site and the card reader
On a booking''s **Money** tab: **Record card payment** records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). **Charge on reader** and **Hold deposit on reader** send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.

## Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)

Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**. A **The deposit hold expires soon** To do opens the booking: **Re-authorize the hold** places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or **Keep part (damage/fees)** for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, **Hold on the card on file**. Under **Money** > **Partner invoices** you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.

## Kickbacks and repairs

**Money** > **Kickbacks and repairs**: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under **Partner invoices** and press **Choose the car**. Add a repair cost with **Add a repair cost**; Fleet adds them on the car''s page too.

### A debit deposit''s card fee
A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable **Card processing fee for a debit deposit**, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## Partners, the timesheet and ended trips

1. **More finance** > **Partners**: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.
2. **Hours** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.
3. **Close ended trips**: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.


## Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release

Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.

1. Open **Money** > **Deposit reviews** and open the booking.
2. Press **Double-check** on each item: read Fleet''s finding and the photos, then **OK** or **Issue** with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.
3. **Highway tolls**: open the toll operator''s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.
4. **Tickets**: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press **None found** or **A ticket**. A ticket is logged in **Tolls and tickets** with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.
5. Then open **Money** on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.

### The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday
On each sweep day a To do **Deposit check sweep** lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. **Deposit reviews** > **This sweep** shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.

### Countdowns
**Money** > **Countdowns** (and the top of **To handle**, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.

### Do sales too
Under **My numbers** > **Do sales too**, press **I want to do sales too**: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.


## The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)

The fuel item shows **Suggested** with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking''s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.

## Statements and payroll (release 35)

- Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.
- Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.
- Field spending (release 50): each expense says whose money paid. You get an alert for each one. **Approve**, or **Decline** with the reason (the person sees it). Own money is then owed to the person: **Reimbursements owed** on Payroll and Field spending lists it per person; press **Mark paid back** once it is paid with their pay.
- Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Payments by e-Transfer or cash, deposits and tips

1. **Record a payment**: a payment of the whole total pays every line of the booking (the rental, short notice, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan), whichever part you record it for. When nothing is open, a booking waiting for payment is confirmed by itself.
2. **The deposit by e-Transfer or cash is doubled**: twice the car''s deposit by default (Program settings). The Security deposit card shows both amounts ("Credit card hold $300.00; e-Transfer or cash $600.00 (2x)"), and the renter sees them on the offer and the pay page before paying.
3. **Collect the deposit** > Cash or e-Transfer: leave the amount empty to take what is owed. Less is recorded as a part (the card says **under, still owed $X** and **Collect the $X still owed** takes the rest); more is held and given back with the deposit (**over, to return $X**).
4. **Change the deposit** on Edit booking (an Admin, with the reason), even while the booking waits for payment: the Money tab, the deposit link and Collect $X deposit follow at once.
5. **Voided a deposit by mistake?** After the void the deposit is **Not collected** again everywhere (the header too): record it again.
6. **Tips**: the renter can add one when paying, on the receipt and from the after-trip email. A tip in cash or by e-Transfer: **Tips** > **Record a tip**. Half goes to the booking''s salesperson and half to the staff member at the handover; with no staff salesperson (a direct booking) CarmaCars keeps that half; one person who did both gets it all. An Admin can give one tip another split (**All to ...**, **Back to the usual split**). A tip is never part of the rental or the owner''s share.
7. A greyed-out button says under it what to do first.

## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

1. A fee waiting for its evidence stays off the statement; the rest goes as usual. Issuing a statement with only such a fee says what is missing.
2. A To do in the Finance queue asks for a toll or ticket notice, a receipt or an invoice. Attach it on the Money tab (**Attach evidence**).
3. When the evidence of a held fee arrives after the Check-out statement, you get **Evidence attached: bill the fee that was waiting**: bill it from the Money tab.
4. Only an Admin charges a fee without its evidence, with the reason.

## Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)

**Money** > **Finance** is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.

1. **Cash position**: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe''s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and **Free cash**: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week''s download.
2. **Money in** and **Money out** for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.
3. **Held for others**: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.
4. **HST** for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.
5. **Renter balances overdue** (past the statement''s 7 days) and **Insurer invoices unpaid** by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).
6. **Twelve months**: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement''s net where one is built.

**Bank lines** is the reconciliation:

1. In RBC online banking open the account, **Download transactions**, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on **Import from RBC online banking**. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.
2. A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.
3. **No match**: **Match** shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. **Set aside** a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. **Undo** takes a reason.
4. A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.

## Check e-Transfer (release 49)

Sales reports an e-Transfer a renter sent, with the screenshot; nothing is recorded until you check the bank. You get an alert and a To do, **Check e-Transfer**.

1. Open the To do: the booking opens on its **Money** tab. The card shows the amount, what it covers, the sender, who reported it and **Open the screenshot**, and says what **Confirm received** will record (for both, the deposit part is the deposit still owed by e-Transfer and the rest is the rental and fees).
2. In the bank: type the **Bank reference (optional)**, then **Confirm received**. It is recorded as Record a payment does (method e-Transfer; your single limit applies) and a booking waiting for payment with nothing open is confirmed. The screenshot becomes the payment''s proof.
3. Not there: **Not received**, say why, **Send back to the rep**. Nothing is recorded; the rep is told.
4. You never check an e-Transfer you reported yourself.
', 'Finance', 'Payments, deposits and refunds, tolls and tickets, reconciliation, the Finance dashboard and Turo trips.',
  'You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. **Money** opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: **To handle** (payments, deposits, refunds), **By day** (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), **All payments**, **Refunds**, **Deposits**, **Reconciliation** and **Unlinked Stripe** (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking''s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking''s payment). **Owner money** lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.

## Your queue

Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.

![The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.](/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 20.3 24.3")

## Payments by day

**Money**, the **By day** tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.

1. Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.
3. At the end of the day count the drawer and press **Record the count**. The difference shows "balanced", or "over" or "short" with the amount.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.

## Payments, deposits, refunds

**Money**, the **To handle** tab.

1. Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank''s reason.
2. Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.
3. Refunds in progress. Press **Request the refund** and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then **Issue the refund**.
4. Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 865; address: carmacars.ca/va/money; pins: 1 10.6 60.3, 2 72.4 21.6, 3 73.2 33.8, 4 11.0 45.9")

## A payment received another way

An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.

1. Owner invoice: on **Payments, deposits, refunds**, find it under Owner invoices owing and press **Record payment**.
2. Renter: beside the failed payment, press **Paid another way**. Or open the booking''s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.
3. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.
4. Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press **Record payment**.

The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.

Each month''s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.


A pay link for the rental, the fees or the balance asks for what is owed and never more (release 48): the booking''s total less every payment of it, refunds counted back. After a change to the total, the link is for the difference. A booking paid in full gets no balance link: anything on top is a later charge, with its reason. A new link replaces any open one for the booking''s money, and a link still open when a payment lands is cancelled by itself (the booking history says so), so the renter is never charged twice.
## Cards, holds and deposits given back

On the booking''s Money tab.

1. After the return, **Charge the renter**: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press **Charge $...**. Before the return, Rental charges, **A later charge**, with the same reason list on the renter''s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, **Charge the card on file as the deposit**.
2. A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or **Release**. **Hold expired**: nothing can be kept from it; press **Charge the card on file instead** (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.
3. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

## Settle a deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (**Keep the whole deposit (damage)**) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## Read a toll notice

1. Open **Tolls and tickets** and press **Read a notice**.
2. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.
3. Press **Read it**. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.
4. Press **Checked against the notice** on each line (**Leave out** to skip one), then **Save as checked** and **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read; pins: 2 19.5 44.1, 3 4.1 64.8, 4 4.1 89.7")

> Tip: In the work queue, **Match again** retries the match after a fix, and **Dispute** marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.

![The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice''s plate, date, amount and match.](/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls; pins: 1 23.6 12.2")

## Reconciliation and Turo trips

1. **Money**, the **Reconciliation** tab: press **Record a processor payout**, then **Match** it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.
2. **Turo trips**: press **Add a trip** for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press **Import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/turo; pins: 2 95.1 14.8")

## Deposits to release

A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: "Release the deposit for" the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.

1. Open the task: it opens the booking''s **Money** tab.
2. Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.
3. The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.

### Card payments outside the site and the card reader
On a booking''s **Money** tab: **Record card payment** records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). **Charge on reader** and **Hold deposit on reader** send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.

## Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)

Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**. A **The deposit hold expires soon** To do opens the booking: **Re-authorize the hold** places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or **Keep part (damage/fees)** for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, **Hold on the card on file**. Under **Money** > **Partner invoices** you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.

## Kickbacks and repairs

**Money** > **Kickbacks and repairs**: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under **Partner invoices** and press **Choose the car**. Add a repair cost with **Add a repair cost**; Fleet adds them on the car''s page too.

### A debit deposit''s card fee
A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable **Card processing fee for a debit deposit**, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## Partners, the timesheet and ended trips

1. **More finance** > **Partners**: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.
2. **Hours** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.
3. **Close ended trips**: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.


## Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release

Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.

1. Open **Money** > **Deposit reviews** and open the booking.
2. Press **Double-check** on each item: read Fleet''s finding and the photos, then **OK** or **Issue** with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.
3. **Highway tolls**: open the toll operator''s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.
4. **Tickets**: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press **None found** or **A ticket**. A ticket is logged in **Tolls and tickets** with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.
5. Then open **Money** on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.

### The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday
On each sweep day a To do **Deposit check sweep** lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. **Deposit reviews** > **This sweep** shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.

### Countdowns
**Money** > **Countdowns** (and the top of **To handle**, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.

### Do sales too
Under **My numbers** > **Do sales too**, press **I want to do sales too**: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.


## The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)

The fuel item shows **Suggested** with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking''s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.

## Statements and payroll (release 35)

- Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.
- Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.
- Field spending (release 50): each expense says whose money paid. You get an alert for each one. **Approve**, or **Decline** with the reason (the person sees it). Own money is then owed to the person: **Reimbursements owed** on Payroll and Field spending lists it per person; press **Mark paid back** once it is paid with their pay.
- Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Payments by e-Transfer or cash, deposits and tips

1. **Record a payment**: a payment of the whole total pays every line of the booking (the rental, short notice, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan), whichever part you record it for. When nothing is open, a booking waiting for payment is confirmed by itself.
2. **The deposit by e-Transfer or cash is doubled**: twice the car''s deposit by default (Program settings). The Security deposit card shows both amounts ("Credit card hold $300.00; e-Transfer or cash $600.00 (2x)"), and the renter sees them on the offer and the pay page before paying.
3. **Collect the deposit** > Cash or e-Transfer: leave the amount empty to take what is owed. Less is recorded as a part (the card says **under, still owed $X** and **Collect the $X still owed** takes the rest); more is held and given back with the deposit (**over, to return $X**).
4. **Change the deposit** on Edit booking (an Admin, with the reason), even while the booking waits for payment: the Money tab, the deposit link and Collect $X deposit follow at once.
5. **Voided a deposit by mistake?** After the void the deposit is **Not collected** again everywhere (the header too): record it again.
6. **Tips**: the renter can add one when paying, on the receipt and from the after-trip email. A tip in cash or by e-Transfer: **Tips** > **Record a tip**. Half goes to the booking''s salesperson and half to the staff member at the handover; with no staff salesperson (a direct booking) CarmaCars keeps that half; one person who did both gets it all. An Admin can give one tip another split (**All to ...**, **Back to the usual split**). A tip is never part of the rental or the owner''s share.
7. A greyed-out button says under it what to do first.

## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

1. A fee waiting for its evidence stays off the statement; the rest goes as usual. Issuing a statement with only such a fee says what is missing.
2. A To do in the Finance queue asks for a toll or ticket notice, a receipt or an invoice. Attach it on the Money tab (**Attach evidence**).
3. When the evidence of a held fee arrives after the Check-out statement, you get **Evidence attached: bill the fee that was waiting**: bill it from the Money tab.
4. Only an Admin charges a fee without its evidence, with the reason.

## Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)

**Money** > **Finance** is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.

1. **Cash position**: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe''s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and **Free cash**: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week''s download.
2. **Money in** and **Money out** for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.
3. **Held for others**: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.
4. **HST** for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.
5. **Renter balances overdue** (past the statement''s 7 days) and **Insurer invoices unpaid** by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).
6. **Twelve months**: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement''s net where one is built.

**Bank lines** is the reconciliation:

1. In RBC online banking open the account, **Download transactions**, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on **Import from RBC online banking**. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.
2. A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.
3. **No match**: **Match** shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. **Set aside** a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. **Undo** takes a reason.
4. A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.

## Check e-Transfer (release 49)

Sales reports an e-Transfer a renter sent, with the screenshot; nothing is recorded until you check the bank. You get an alert and a To do, **Check e-Transfer**.

1. Open the To do: the booking opens on its **Money** tab. The card shows the amount, what it covers, the sender, who reported it and **Open the screenshot**, and says what **Confirm received** will record (for both, the deposit part is the deposit still owed by e-Transfer and the rest is the rental and fees).
2. In the bank: type the **Bank reference (optional)**, then **Confirm received**. It is recorded as Record a payment does (method e-Transfer; your single limit applies) and a booking waiting for payment with nothing open is confirmed. The screenshot becomes the payment''s proof.
3. Not there: **Not received**, say why, **Send back to the rep**. Nothing is recorded; the rep is told.
4. You never check an e-Transfer you reported yourself.


## 407 ETR statements

1. Read the statement PDF or its CSV download (the PDF and the CSV of one statement are the same trips: read one of them).
2. Each trip is read from its column: the date and the entry time, the plate (from its own column, or the Licence Plate line above its trips), the entry and the exit, and the toll with its camera and trip toll charges. The line''s amount is what the renter owes for the trip; Of which fees is the camera and trip toll charges. A distance is never read as money.
3. The monthly account fee and a late payment charge are not trips: they are listed under the read as left out.
4. A credit or a reversal is left out and said. A line whose charges do not add up to its total is marked for you to check.
5. Each trip goes to whoever had the car at that minute. Within the boundary margin of Program settings (30 minutes) of a rental''s start or end, a person confirms who had it; nothing is charged by itself there.

## Log an expense from the receipt

**More finance** > **Maintenance and expenses** > **Expenses**, on a phone or a computer.

1. Press **Take a photo** (or **Upload photos**). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.
2. The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.
3. Who pays: the car''s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick **I paid with my own money** to be paid back.
4. Press **Save**. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.

## Winter tire fee on a rental

Open the booking. The **Winter tire fee** card sets this rental''s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.

1. It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer''s invoice).
2. The change is kept in the booking''s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> (payments, deposits, refunds), <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), <b class="gd-ui">All payments</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Refunds</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposits</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Unlinked Stripe</b> (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking&#39;s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking&#39;s payment). <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b> lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.</p><section class="gd-task" id="finance-your-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg" alt="The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.3%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At the end of the day count the drawer and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>. The difference shows &quot;balanced&quot;, or &quot;over&quot; or &quot;short&quot; with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-deposits-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments, deposits, refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds in progress. Press <b class="gd-ui">Request the refund</b> and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/money</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/865"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="865"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.6%;top:60.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.4%;top:21.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:45.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-payment-received-another-way" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A payment received another way</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoice: on <b class="gd-ui">Payments, deposits, refunds</b>, find it under Owner invoices owing and press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Renter: beside the failed payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>. Or open the booking&#39;s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.</p><p class="gd-p">Each month&#39;s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.</p><p class="gd-p">A pay link for the rental, the fees or the balance asks for what is owed and never more (release 48): the booking&#39;s total less every payment of it, refunds counted back. After a change to the total, the link is for the difference. A booking paid in full gets no balance link: anything on top is a later charge, with its reason. A new link replaces any open one for the booking&#39;s money, and a link still open when a payment lands is cancelled by itself (the booking history says so), so the renter is never charged twice.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-cards-holds-and-deposits-given-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cards, holds and deposits given back</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After the return, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge $...</b>. Before the return, Rental charges, <b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b>, with the same reason list on the renter&#39;s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or <b class="gd-ui">Release</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hold expired</b>: nothing can be kept from it; press <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file instead</b> (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-settle-a-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle a deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-out statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (<b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b>) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-read-a-toll-notice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read a toll notice</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Read a notice</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked against the notice</b> on each line (<b class="gd-ui">Leave out</b> to skip one), then <b class="gd-ui">Save as checked</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Confirm and import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/580"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="580"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.5%;top:44.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:64.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>In the work queue, <b class="gd-ui">Match again</b> retries the match after a fix, and <b class="gd-ui">Dispute</b> marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg" alt="The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:12.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-reconciliation-and-turo-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reconciliation and Turo trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> tab: press <b class="gd-ui">Record a processor payout</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turo trips</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Add a trip</b> for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/turo</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.1%;top:14.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposits-to-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits to release</h2><p class="gd-p">A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: &quot;Release the deposit for&quot; the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task: it opens the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Card payments outside the site and the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: <b class="gd-ui">Record card payment</b> records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). <b class="gd-ui">Charge on reader</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Hold deposit on reader</b> send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposit-holds-and-partner-invoices-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold not re-authorized</b>. A <b class="gd-ui">The deposit hold expires soon</b> To do opens the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b> places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, <b class="gd-ui">Hold on the card on file</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partner invoices</b> you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-kickbacks-and-repairs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Kickbacks and repairs</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b>: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under <b class="gd-ui">Partner invoices</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Choose the car</b>. Add a repair cost with <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>; Fleet adds them on the car&#39;s page too.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A debit deposit&#39;s card fee</h3><p class="gd-p">A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</b>, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-partners-the-timesheet-and-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Partners, the timesheet and ended trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">More finance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposit-review-double-check-tolls-and-tickets-then-bill-or-r" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release</h2><p class="gd-p">Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> and open the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Double-check</b> on each item: read Fleet&#39;s finding and the photos, then <b class="gd-ui">OK</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Issue</b> with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Highway tolls</b>: open the toll operator&#39;s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tickets</b>: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press <b class="gd-ui">None found</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A ticket</b>. A ticket is logged in <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday</h3><p class="gd-p">On each sweep day a To do <b class="gd-ui">Deposit check sweep</b> lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">This sweep</b> shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Countdowns</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Countdowns</b> (and the top of <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b>, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Do sales too</h3><p class="gd-p">Under <b class="gd-ui">My numbers</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Do sales too</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">I want to do sales too</b>: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-the-fuel-line-on-the-deposit-review-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The fuel item shows <b class="gd-ui">Suggested</b> with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking&#39;s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-statements-and-payroll-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payroll (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.</li><li>Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.</li><li>Field spending (release 50): each expense says whose money paid. You get an alert for each one. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason (the person sees it). Own money is then owed to the person: <b class="gd-ui">Reimbursements owed</b> on Payroll and Field spending lists it per person; press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid back</b> once it is paid with their pay.</li><li>Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-e-transfer-or-cash-deposits-and-tips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by e-Transfer or cash, deposits and tips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: a payment of the whole total pays every line of the booking (the rental, short notice, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan), whichever part you record it for. When nothing is open, a booking waiting for payment is confirmed by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The deposit by e-Transfer or cash is doubled</b>: twice the car&#39;s deposit by default (Program settings). The Security deposit card shows both amounts (&quot;Credit card hold $300.00; e-Transfer or cash $600.00 (2x)&quot;), and the renter sees them on the offer and the pay page before paying.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Collect the deposit</b> &gt; Cash or e-Transfer: leave the amount empty to take what is owed. Less is recorded as a part (the card says <b class="gd-ui">under, still owed $X</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Collect the $X still owed</b> takes the rest); more is held and given back with the deposit (<b class="gd-ui">over, to return $X</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change the deposit</b> on Edit booking (an Admin, with the reason), even while the booking waits for payment: the Money tab, the deposit link and Collect $X deposit follow at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Voided a deposit by mistake?</b> After the void the deposit is <b class="gd-ui">Not collected</b> again everywhere (the header too): record it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tips</b>: the renter can add one when paying, on the receipt and from the after-trip email. A tip in cash or by e-Transfer: <b class="gd-ui">Tips</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Record a tip</b>. Half goes to the booking&#39;s salesperson and half to the staff member at the handover; with no staff salesperson (a direct booking) CarmaCars keeps that half; one person who did both gets it all. An Admin can give one tip another split (<b class="gd-ui">All to ...</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the usual split</b>). A tip is never part of the rental or the owner&#39;s share.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A greyed-out button says under it what to do first.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-evidence-for-every-fee-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Evidence for every fee (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A fee waiting for its evidence stays off the statement; the rest goes as usual. Issuing a statement with only such a fee says what is missing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A To do in the Finance queue asks for a toll or ticket notice, a receipt or an invoice. Attach it on the Money tab (<b class="gd-ui">Attach evidence</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the evidence of a held fee arrives after the Check-out statement, you get <b class="gd-ui">Evidence attached: bill the fee that was waiting</b>: bill it from the Money tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Only an Admin charges a fee without its evidence, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-finance-dashboard-and-the-bank-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b> is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cash position</b>: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe&#39;s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and <b class="gd-ui">Free cash</b>: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week&#39;s download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money in</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Money out</b> for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Held for others</b>: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">HST</b> for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter balances overdue</b> (past the statement&#39;s 7 days) and <b class="gd-ui">Insurer invoices unpaid</b> by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Twelve months</b>: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement&#39;s net where one is built.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bank lines</b> is the reconciliation:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In RBC online banking open the account, <b class="gd-ui">Download transactions</b>, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on <b class="gd-ui">Import from RBC online banking</b>. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">No match</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b> a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-check-e-transfer-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check e-Transfer (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p">Sales reports an e-Transfer a renter sent, with the screenshot; nothing is recorded until you check the bank. You get an alert and a To do, <b class="gd-ui">Check e-Transfer</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the To do: the booking opens on its <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab. The card shows the amount, what it covers, the sender, who reported it and <b class="gd-ui">Open the screenshot</b>, and says what <b class="gd-ui">Confirm received</b> will record (for both, the deposit part is the deposit still owed by e-Transfer and the rest is the rental and fees).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In the bank: type the <b class="gd-ui">Bank reference (optional)</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm received</b>. It is recorded as Record a payment does (method e-Transfer; your single limit applies) and a booking waiting for payment with nothing open is confirmed. The screenshot becomes the payment&#39;s proof.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not there: <b class="gd-ui">Not received</b>, say why, <b class="gd-ui">Send back to the rep</b>. Nothing is recorded; the rep is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">You never check an e-Transfer you reported yourself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-407-etr-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">407 ETR statements</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Read the statement PDF or its CSV download (the PDF and the CSV of one statement are the same trips: read one of them).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each trip is read from its column: the date and the entry time, the plate (from its own column, or the Licence Plate line above its trips), the entry and the exit, and the toll with its camera and trip toll charges. The line&#39;s amount is what the renter owes for the trip; Of which fees is the camera and trip toll charges. A distance is never read as money.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly account fee and a late payment charge are not trips: they are listed under the read as left out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A credit or a reversal is left out and said. A line whose charges do not add up to its total is marked for you to check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each trip goes to whoever had the car at that minute. Within the boundary margin of Program settings (30 minutes) of a rental&#39;s start or end, a person confirms who had it; nothing is charged by itself there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-log-an-expense-from-the-receipt" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Log an expense from the receipt</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More finance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance and expenses</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Expenses</b>, on a phone or a computer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Upload photos</b>). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the car&#39;s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick <b class="gd-ui">I paid with my own money</b> to be paid back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-winter-tire-fee-on-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Winter tire fee on a rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the booking. The <b class="gd-ui">Winter tire fee</b> card sets this rental&#39;s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer&#39;s invoice).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The change is kept in the booking&#39;s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")


### Shifts in your Google Calendar

At the bottom of **Field jobs** (and on your **Profile**), **Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: who claimed it or Open, the tasks and a link to it, and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. Google refreshes it every few hours on its own. **Regenerate link** stops the old link; **Turn off** stops it.

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1940 Eglinton Ave E; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site). The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.
## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.

## One look: studio renders only (release 50)

The site shows only studio renders that passed the studio gate (the same car size, position, room, floor and shadow for every car): the car page, the cards, the home page, the feeds and the emails. A car with none yet shows one **Photos coming soon** photo; its own photos are never shown to the public but stay on the car''s record. **Photo standard** > **Studio grid** shows every car''s nine views side by side with **Live**, **Gate refused** or **Flagged** and why.

## Sign first, then cars

An owner''s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car''s Schedule A entry. On the owner''s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car''s tier and plate.

A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as "Pickup not recorded, car presumed out": record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.

## Check-in visits (release 50)

A renter on a long rental (28 days or more, a long-term weekly rental, or a rideshare driver) is asked to bring the car in about once a month. It is a suggestion, never a requirement and never a fee.

1. Open **Checks** > **Check-in visits**. **Booked** comes first, then **Due**, **Overdue** (soft: a friendly call is fine) and **Done**. You get an email and a notice when a renter picks a time, and the morning of a visit.
2. Press **Do the visit**: take the five photos (front, rear, left side, right side, odometer), type the odometer, say whether there is new damage (where and what), the tire tread in mm, whether the fluids look right and any warning light, and notes.
3. Press **Save the visit**. The reading and the tread go into the car''s maintenance, which shows the next service due. Anything to look after (a service due, tread under 3 mm, fluids, a warning light) becomes a Fleet To do; damage is logged on the Damage tab with an Admin To do.
4. **Book a time for the renter** picks an office slot for them; **Skip this month** needs the reason; **Start a visit now** is for a renter who drops by.

On the booking page, **Check-in visits** shows the next one and turns them on for any rental, off for this one, or back to the rule.
', 'Fleet', 'Field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews, similar cars and listings.',
  'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")


### Shifts in your Google Calendar

At the bottom of **Field jobs** (and on your **Profile**), **Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: who claimed it or Open, the tasks and a link to it, and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. Google refreshes it every few hours on its own. **Regenerate link** stops the old link; **Turn off** stops it.

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1940 Eglinton Ave E; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site). The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.
## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.

## One look: studio renders only (release 50)

The site shows only studio renders that passed the studio gate (the same car size, position, room, floor and shadow for every car): the car page, the cards, the home page, the feeds and the emails. A car with none yet shows one **Photos coming soon** photo; its own photos are never shown to the public but stay on the car''s record. **Photo standard** > **Studio grid** shows every car''s nine views side by side with **Live**, **Gate refused** or **Flagged** and why.

## Sign first, then cars

An owner''s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car''s Schedule A entry. On the owner''s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car''s tier and plate.

A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as "Pickup not recorded, car presumed out": record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.

## Check-in visits (release 50)

A renter on a long rental (28 days or more, a long-term weekly rental, or a rideshare driver) is asked to bring the car in about once a month. It is a suggestion, never a requirement and never a fee.

1. Open **Checks** > **Check-in visits**. **Booked** comes first, then **Due**, **Overdue** (soft: a friendly call is fine) and **Done**. You get an email and a notice when a renter picks a time, and the morning of a visit.
2. Press **Do the visit**: take the five photos (front, rear, left side, right side, odometer), type the odometer, say whether there is new damage (where and what), the tire tread in mm, whether the fluids look right and any warning light, and notes.
3. Press **Save the visit**. The reading and the tread go into the car''s maintenance, which shows the next service due. Anything to look after (a service due, tread under 3 mm, fluids, a warning light) becomes a Fleet To do; damage is logged on the Damage tab with an Admin To do.
4. **Book a time for the renter** picks an office slot for them; **Skip this month** needs the reason; **Start a visit now** is for a renter who drops by.

On the booking page, **Check-in visits** shows the next one and turns them on for any rental, off for this one, or back to the rule.


## Log an expense from the receipt

**Maintenance** > **Expenses**, on a phone or a computer.

1. Press **Take a photo** (or **Upload photos**). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.
2. The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.
3. Who pays: the car''s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick **I paid with my own money** to be paid back.
4. Press **Save**. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.

## Ownership documents in bulk

**More fleet** > **Listings** > **Ownership documents**

1. Press **Choose the files** and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.
2. Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press **File it on this car**. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.
3. A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press **File it on this car**, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-schedule-field-jobs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Schedule field jobs</h2><p class="gd-p">Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking&#39;s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day&#39;s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. &quot;Made from the booking&quot; marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Change a job with <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> (another shift), <b class="gd-ui">Assign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), <b class="gd-ui">Move</b> (time and place) or <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b>, the place filled in from the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings &gt; Program.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/fleet</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/565"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="565"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.9%;top:51.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Shifts in your Google Calendar</h3><p class="gd-p">At the bottom of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b> (and on your <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>), <b class="gd-ui">Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar</b> gives you a private link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: who claimed it or Open, the tasks and a link to it, and the weekly townhall. Press <b class="gd-ui">Make my calendar link</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add to Google Calendar</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> in Google. Google refreshes it every few hours on its own. <b class="gd-ui">Regenerate link</b> stops the old link; <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Shifts, next seven days</b> shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (<b class="gd-ui">Jobs on it</b>). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Need more? Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>: the first day&#39;s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a person</b> puts someone on a shift and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking&#39;s real time; the renter&#39;s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> takes a job off its person and its shift; tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-missing-check-ins-and-check-outs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing check-ins and check-outs</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b> on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b> and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-fleet-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet map</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin&#39;s. Every staff member sees the cars&#39; positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Car map</b>), read only, and field staff under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car page and booking page shows <b class="gd-ui">Where the car is</b>: moving or parked, when it last reported and <b class="gd-ui">Open on the map</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>. Only Admins and fleet staff press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-hours" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field hours</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Field hours</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clocked in now</b> lists who is on, since when. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between pay periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock out: press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out for them</b>, set the time they finished and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Where they clocked in</h3><p class="gd-p">The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-daily-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Daily checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Daily checks</b> and choose <b class="gd-ui">Opening check</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Closing check</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the opening check</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Save the closing check</b>). You can save it again.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/checks</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/820"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.5%;top:15.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:44.7%;top:42%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:64.2%;top:94%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking press <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b>; on a booking on rent, <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Afterwards press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> and a reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-photo-reviews-after-a-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photo reviews after a return</h2><p class="gd-p">After each return, the field photo set waits under <b class="gd-ui">Photo reviews</b>. Compare it with the pickup set. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review done</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a re-shoot</b> if a photo is missing or unclear.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-similar-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Similar cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car&#39;s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> with a note when they are different cars, or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b> when they are.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/460"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="460"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">From a listing, press <b class="gd-ui">The car and its rates</b>, or open the car from Field jobs and its <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> for the kilometres, or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check What renters pay under the fields, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-listings-and-covering-plates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listings and covering plates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/340"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="340"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:54.5%;top:49.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The listing&#39;s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>: the editor opens under the photo; <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/776"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="776"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.6%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.5%;top:62.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:43.1%;top:92.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-missing-angles-and-short-videos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing angles and short videos</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press <b class="gd-ui">Make</b> and the angle (for example <b class="gd-ui">Make Rear</b>): the image model makes the view from the car&#39;s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make a short video</b> for a 9:16 video of the car&#39;s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-publish-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-in: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">An urgent To do &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot; means the renter pressed <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter&#39;s photos), then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> takes the VIN from the car: <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> in the door frame or under the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>; drag the extras into their order in the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo&#39;s edge is cut off by itself. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b>, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model&#39;s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b> does every car. Under a photo, <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again and <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before. <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b> on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>); the website&#39;s photos stay as they are. <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b> on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: <b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">With a model</b> (the image model&#39;s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or <b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b> (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-screen-many-photos-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One screen, many photos (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b> on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.</p><p class="gd-p">Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter&#39;s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car&#39;s page, record <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Return to owner</b> with photos: the owner sees them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-repair-costs-on-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repair costs on a car</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b>, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> prints that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-government-forms-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Government forms (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-odometer-and-fuel-at-every-check-in-and-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photo of the dashboard</b>: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Selfie in front of the car</b>: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking&#39;s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car&#39;s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-change-the-car-of-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change the car of a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b>, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car&#39;s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-an-accident-reported-by-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An accident reported by a renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-payments-and-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments and calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet takes payments on a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.</p><p class="gd-p">Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and <b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calls and texts</b> is your inbox. A car late back has <b class="gd-ui">Returning now</b> on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.</p><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> beside the form (who, when, the version) and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> and the owner is asked to sign again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-close-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Close ended trips</h2><p class="gd-p">A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has <b class="gd-ui">Mark settled (released by expiry)</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-the-primary-photo-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag <b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. <b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b>. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> card on Listings: each car&#39;s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b>. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-applicant-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field applicant calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. <b class="gd-ui">Field applicant calls</b> on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-value-and-fuel-on-the-car-page-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Value and fuel</b>:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Canadian Black Book value</b> (with the date checked) or an <b class="gd-ui">Estimated value (when no Black Book)</b>: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Tank (litres)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Fuel grade</b> (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or <b class="gd-ui">Battery (kWh)</b> for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-delivery-and-fuel-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The shift board shows each field person&#39;s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.</li><li>You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.</li><li>Delivery is priced by distance from 1940 Eglinton Ave E; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.</li><li>An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-every-view-generated-from-the-car-s-photos-release-47" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every view generated from the car&#39;s photos (release 47)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car&#39;s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site). The real photos stay on the car&#39;s record. On <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Generated set</b> shows each car&#39;s views made out of nine; <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> makes them again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-picked-up-deposit-pending-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open <b class="gd-ui">Let the car go with the deposit owed</b>, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now</b> has the box <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because</b>, and the check-in panel has <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it</b>. The booking then shows <b class="gd-ui">Deposit pending $X</b> everywhere. Each morning the renter&#39;s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-studio-renders-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio renders (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car&#39;s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.</li><li>Renders go live by themselves. You get &quot;Studio photos live&quot; in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.</li><li>Something is off: open the car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b>.</li><li>To render every published car now: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Render every published car</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-evidence-for-every-fee-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Evidence for every fee (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking&#39;s Money tab, <b class="gd-ui">Evidence for every fee</b> lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled &quot;Field:&quot; when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Attach evidence</b> on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a return charge</b>: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter&#39;s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-tracker-events-and-pound-flags-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b>, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car&#39;s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b>; you do not.</li><li>Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.</li><li>A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">A car that leaves Ontario or Canada</b>: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: a car parked at a known pound.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an urgent To do and alert. Open <b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: the lot&#39;s phone and hours are on the row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the path</b> and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), <b class="gd-ui">Recovered, nothing to charge</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not a pound</b>. Write what happened in a sentence.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b> are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot&#39;s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-look-studio-renders-only-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One look: studio renders only (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">The site shows only studio renders that passed the studio gate (the same car size, position, room, floor and shadow for every car): the car page, the cards, the home page, the feeds and the emails. A car with none yet shows one <b class="gd-ui">Photos coming soon</b> photo; its own photos are never shown to the public but stay on the car&#39;s record. <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Studio grid</b> shows every car&#39;s nine views side by side with <b class="gd-ui">Live</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Gate refused</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Flagged</b> and why.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car&#39;s Schedule A entry. On the owner&#39;s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car&#39;s tier and plate.</p><p class="gd-p">A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as &quot;Pickup not recorded, car presumed out&quot;: record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-in-visits-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in visits (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter on a long rental (28 days or more, a long-term weekly rental, or a rideshare driver) is asked to bring the car in about once a month. It is a suggestion, never a requirement and never a fee.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checks</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Booked</b> comes first, then <b class="gd-ui">Due</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Overdue</b> (soft: a friendly call is fine) and <b class="gd-ui">Done</b>. You get an email and a notice when a renter picks a time, and the morning of a visit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Do the visit</b>: take the five photos (front, rear, left side, right side, odometer), type the odometer, say whether there is new damage (where and what), the tire tread in mm, whether the fluids look right and any warning light, and notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the visit</b>. The reading and the tread go into the car&#39;s maintenance, which shows the next service due. Anything to look after (a service due, tread under 3 mm, fluids, a warning light) becomes a Fleet To do; damage is logged on the Damage tab with an Admin To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Book a time for the renter</b> picks an office slot for them; <b class="gd-ui">Skip this month</b> needs the reason; <b class="gd-ui">Start a visit now</b> is for a renter who drops by.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b> shows the next one and turns them on for any rental, off for this one, or back to the rule.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-log-an-expense-from-the-receipt" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Log an expense from the receipt</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Expenses</b>, on a phone or a computer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Upload photos</b>). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the car&#39;s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick <b class="gd-ui">I paid with my own money</b> to be paid back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-ownership-documents-in-bulk" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ownership documents in bulk</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Ownership documents</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Choose the files</b> and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">File it on this car</b>. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press <b class="gd-ui">File it on this car</b>, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'car-maintenance', 'chapter', 'assistant', 'Fleet keeps every car serviced: oil, tires, brakes, inspections and the registration. Finance bills what Fleet records. Recording a service resets its reminders and makes its bill.

## What is due

Open **Field work** > **Maintenance** (Finance: **Money** > **Maintenance bills**).

1. Every car, most urgent first: overdue (red), due soon, no record yet (dashed), all OK.
2. Your To do has one Service due task per car listing what is due. Open it: the car opens with the record pop-up.
3. A car with no record yet has one task to record its last service. Enter what you know once.

## Record a service

1. Press **Record a service** on the car (or **Record** on one item of the car''s Maintenance).
2. Tick what was done, check the date and the odometer, type the shop, the cost before HST and the HST, and add the receipt.
3. Who pays: the owner for an owner''s car (deducted on their statement), CarmaCars for a company car, a claim, the renter, or no charge.
4. Leave **The bill is in: bill it now** ticked, or untick it and press **Bill now** on the record later.
5. Press **Record the service**. The items done are OK again.

> Watch out: Above your single limit the service is recorded and the timers reset, but an Admin bills it: you see "An Admin bills it".

## Tires, swaps and readings

- Under Tires: **Add a tire set** (kind, size, brand, tread, made and bought dates, where it is stored), **Put on the car** to swap.
- Ontario: winter tires on by December 1 (reminder from November 1), off after April 1. Tires are due soon at 4 mm of tread, overdue at 3 mm.
- **Add a reading** when you see the odometer. Handover, return and move readings come in by themselves.
- A car whose recorded safety inspection or registration has expired cannot be handed over until the renewal is recorded.
', 'Car maintenance', 'The maintenance list, recording a service in one step, tires and swaps, readings, and billing.',
